{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance","id":1318100,"title":"Houserules for Artifacts and Resonance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-12T13:13:25-07:00","id":1318100,"title":"Houserules for Artifacts and Resonance","content":"As things stand now, we have a situation where there are artifacts that are resonant, dissonant and neutral with some exalted types, but they cost exactly the same, be their costs as merits, or their evocations. This is not a problem for the solars, who are resonant with everything. But for other exalted, it leaves something to be desired. It discourages the purchase of out of type artifacts, and that reduces the value of artifact companions such as Arms of the Chosen, because they come with very few artifacts of the same material.<br /> <br /> What I want to accomplish is to make varied artifacts a little more 'cost-beneficial', and less of an explicitly bad idea. If you have a concept that makes for your character having an out-of-type artifact, you shouldn't have to be penalized for this.<ul><li>The artifact merit costs one point less for out-of-type materials. <i>So, a dragonblooded that got a level 3 starmetal artifact gets to pay 2 dots at character creation, not three. </i>T<i>his represents the fact that such artifacts are not so desirable for the characters and in-universe, as equivalent artifacts of the correct material. </i></li> <li>Evocations can be purchased in three levels: Dissonant level costs &lt;normal cost -2&gt;xp, Neutral level cost &lt;normal cost&gt; xp, and Resonant level costs &lt;normal cost + 2&gt; xp. <i>This is evocation by evocation - evocations that don't have a resonant or dissonant effect are, by definition, neutral.</i></li> </ul>For extra flexibility, a character may even choose to attune with a lower level of an evocation. For instance, he could purchase an evocation at dissonant level, for less XP, and later (if the evocation has a resonant level and is resonant with the character) upgrade it to a higher level by paying the difference. <br /> <br /> So what are your ideas on that?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T13:33:15-07:00","id":1318105,"title":"","content":"The great majority of our Artifacts are bespoke written for the characters who bear them. As such, they don't have Resonant or Dissonant keywords. ( &quot;I'm writing my signature weapon to be <i>cooler </i>in the hands of somebody else!&quot;) <br /> <br /> We also have a table understanding that we're not doing a high-fatality game (so we can explore more character dramas) nor a steal-your-stuff game (so variations in resonance don't mean as much). <br /> <br /> The only specific house rule we've had to do was to replace the Lunars' DBT penalty for Resonance. We'll be testing a 1m / turn cost to maintain DBT to replace the Resonance drawback. We might just disregard it entirely and assume that Resonance and Dissonance are present in the Artifact, but don't affect the same character as long as they consistently own it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:17:06-07:00","id":1318112,"title":"","content":"Also just because an artifact is <i>slightly less</i> powerful in your hands doesn\u2019t make it <i>not powerful</i>, considering how getting to explore a set of powers outside your normal themes is worthy of consideration all on its own. A Dragon-Blooded wielding Gnomon is not particularly missing out on anything just because she\u2019s not as good with it as a Solar is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-12-2019, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:17:25-07:00","id":1318113,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, we could each build our artifacts and evocations. But it'd be like, work. And, I like the flavor of dissonant/resonant effects. So, we tend to mostly use published artifacts and stick to those rules otherwise. <br /> <br /> I had the idea of working with resonance and dissonance when two players from my group built lunars that had killed Dragonbloded on their backgrounds. One of them wanted to purchase an artifact from this story, but then it'd be more than likely jade. So, I started to think: how would I not penalize her by doing that? How would I interest a player in investing in evocations from an artifact that isn't 'optimal'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:25:22-07:00","id":1318116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318112#post1318112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also just because an artifact is <i>slightly less</i> powerful in your hands doesn\u2019t make it <i>not powerful</i>, considering how getting to explore a set of powers outside your normal themes is worthy of consideration all on its own. A Dragon-Blooded wielding Gnomon is not particularly missing out on anything just because she\u2019s not as good with it as a Solar is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Dragonblooded with Gnomon won't access several evocations, and can't have the peaches. The! Peaches! Of! Immortality! I can't even parse your argument!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:30:30-07:00","id":1318120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318116#post1318116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A Dragonblooded with Gnomon won't access several evocations, and can't have the peaches. The! Peaches! Of! Immortality! I can't even parse your argument!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Solution: &quot;Uh, guys, this is totally not Gnomon, this is its Blue Jade brother Chronos. Totally guys. Swear on me mum. Has all of Gnomon's Evocations and pretty much works the same way though.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:56:55-07:00","id":1318131,"title":"","content":"Some things to consider :<br /> <br /> -I don't think it makes sense to reduce the dot cost of the artifact, since only the evocations are weaker. The artifact still has its maximum number of Evocation and the general scope of its powers determined by its dot rating. Reduced cost per Evocation makes sense though.<br /> <br /> -Since you're not interested in creating custom Evocations and the artifact isn't likely to be used by someone else, I'd recommend simply treating the player as resonant out of game and calling it a day.<br /> <br /> -Since your player is a Lunar, one way you could solve the problem would be to give them a custom (Wits - Cache) Charm that makes them resonant with an artifact if they own the shape of a previous owner who was resonant with it. Or simply houserule that all Lunars can do that if you don't want to bother with a custom Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T15:00:00-07:00","id":1318133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318116#post1318116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dragonblooded with Gnomon won't access several evocations, and can't have the peaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the Evocations that even two people of the same splat get with the same weapon won\u2019t be identical; the way they\u2019re presented to us is meant to be there as guidelines. Nobody will get all the possible Evocations of an artifact because the bond an artifact develops with a wielder is going to be dependent on their relationship.<br /> <br /> Second, so what? He\u2019s still capable of interrupting an enemy\u2019s charge to dig a pit filled with sharpened sticks at the bottom. Out of the two I\u2019d argue that\u2019s the more impressive feat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318116#post1318116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't even parse your argument!</div> </div> </div> </div>Try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-12-2019, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T15:10:10-07:00","id":1318137,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd rather just ignore Resonance/Dissonance if I felt like it/the PC convinced me. It's not really like the balance is so fine on the artifacts that it really screws with stuff. All it does is mucks with Solars being the best at everything.... which is a feature as far as I'm concerned, not a bug! :P (And they still have extra charms on pretty much every artifact in Arms anyway)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T16:20:13-07:00","id":1318149,"title":"","content":"So I had an idea after rereading through all the ideas here. <br /> <br /> What if.... Dissonance was presented along the lines of being a Flaw? If you're Dissonant with one of your Artifacts, and it has an effect at a dramatic moment, you can take a penalty in exchange for an Exalted XP. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T17:14:58-07:00","id":1318152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318149#post1318149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I had an idea after rereading through all the ideas here.<br /> <br /> What if.... Dissonance was presented along the lines of being a Flaw? If you're Dissonant with one of your Artifacts, and it has an effect at a dramatic moment, you can take a penalty in exchange for an Exalted XP.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually a neat idea~ Though I doubt being Dissonant with an Artifact will often lead to dramatic moments, considering it's a small distinction usually, and you can't really say &quot;Drat! If I had had this neutral-locked Evocation I would have succeeded at X!&quot; most of the time either. I'd just treat it as a Flaw that comes online when you use a Dissonant-tagged Evocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T17:25:13-07:00","id":1318154,"title":"","content":"Love the idea of a Dissonance flaw.<br /> <br /> Here are some other ideas for alternate Resonance rules :<br /> <br /> -Simple no-nonsense rule : Resonance is a 3 or 5 Dot Merit you can purchase for each Artifact, where 3 Dot = Neutral and 5 Dot = Resonant. If your character is neutral/resonant with an Artifact you simply get the appropriate Merit for free for that Artifact.<br /> <br /> -More involved rule : While you are attuned to an artifact it gains normal exp when you do. When you reach 50 normal exp with an Artifact its affinity goes up 1 level. So a dissonant E1 Artifact becomes neutral after 50 exp and then Resonant after another 50 exp.<br /> <br /> -Harsher rule : For each Essence level you have above an Evocation's Essence requirement, you gain 1 level of affinity for that Evocation. For instance, a dissonant E1 Evocation becomes Neutral when you hit Essence 2 and Resonant when you hit Essence 3. So everyone can use an Artifact to its full potential but it takes longer for those who aren't Resonant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T18:33:16-07:00","id":1318165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318152#post1318152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's actually a neat idea~ Though I doubt being Dissonant with an Artifact will often lead to dramatic moments, considering it's a small distinction usually, and you can't really say &quot;Drat! If I had had this neutral-locked Evocation I would have succeeded at X!&quot; most of the time either. I'd just treat it as a Flaw that comes online when you use a Dissonant-tagged Evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea would most definitely need some development!<br /> <br /> How can Dissonance be part of the story, rather than a bit of crunch, I wonder? What does Dissonance feel like? Could it be a stunt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T19:45:07-07:00","id":1318167,"title":"","content":"My house rule for Resonance is that you can be Resonant to any artifact that contains a magical material you are Resonant to.<br /> <br /> For instance, a weapon that is a Moonsilver and Jade Daiklave is resonant to Solars, Lunars, and Dragonblooded, plus any Exigent who is Resonant to Moonsilver or Jade.<br /> <br /> The idea to me is that this encourages a player to think about how a different magical material interacts both with them as a splat and their magical material. It lets them look for overlapping themes and how one material encourages another, without limiting them on how they pick a weapon. Too much freedom to me creates a mush that isn't super enticing, while slightly stretching the boundaries or playing with how a weapon might change by you adding a new magical material to it to better attune to it, what Evocations might be empowered nad what might reduce.<br /> <br /> Admittedly I love making artifacts so often what happens is that I make the artifacts and evocations for everyone that have ideas of themes and paths to explore and see where my players want to take them. Usually they'll say what kind of weapon they want and a brief overview of the powers it should have and I'll make an artifact for them in response.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T08:32:51-07:00","id":1318231,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not really bothered; my game is a Lunar game, so they're only Resonant with Moonsilver artefacts, but the Lunar book has a ton of moonsilver artefacts in anyway. Similarly, the Dragonblood book has 11 Jade artefacts.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's going to break stuff if you make evocations a little cheaper when they're dissonant, but as Epitome pointed out, letting Dragonblood buy non-Jade daiklaives for 2 dots is a bit cheap; I mean, a daiklaive is way better than most 2-dot artefacts, even if you don't buy any artefacts.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that because of the way the themes of materials line up with the themes of that splat, they can sometimes be a bit less useful for that splat anyway.<br /> <br /> For example, the black jade crossbow in Arms lets you run on water... which Water Aspects can do anyway. Its charms for helping with Naval Combat are much more useful for a Lunar than a DB, because DBs have a bunch of other charms to help with Naval Combat, and Lunars don't.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of kitting out a DB NPC with the red jade bow that shoots emotions into people, but I realised that DBs have loads of charms for inspiring emotions anyway. It's probably more useful for a Sidereal (and indeed, that's who's wielding it in the art).<br /> <br /> The Jade firewand and Jade flamepiece in Arms start off with an evocation that lets you reload a firewand reflexively; something DBs have an Archery charm for anyway, something I expect that Abyssals, Liminals and Sidereals won't have.<br /> <br /> The soulsteel mace that lets you trap ghosts and learn magic from an ancient ghost is probably less useful for an Abyssal (who probably knows a bunch of ghosts anyway, and likely has plenty of charms for dealing with them) and more useful for a Sidereal or Alchemical, who don't really have that much.<br /> <br /> And the most obvious example is the Moonsilver cloak which turns into wings; much less useful for the splat that can already grow wings (Lunars) than the ones who can't (Solars, DBs, Sidereals, Liminals, most Exigents, Abyssals... I guess Alchemicals possibly can).<br /> <br /> This isn't always the case; having a flying sword that can attack by itself or a sword-loom that can produce cloth-servitors or just as useful for Lunars as they are for anyone else.<br /> But it's something to bear in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T11:09:26-07:00","id":1318263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318131#post1318131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things to consider :<br /> <br /> -I don't think it makes sense to reduce the dot cost of the artifact, since only the evocations are weaker. The artifact still has its maximum number of Evocation and the general scope of its powers determined by its dot rating. Reduced cost per Evocation makes sense though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maximum Number of Evocations per Dot Rating? Where would I find that information? I Must have completely missed this... <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T15:55:48-07:00","id":1318326,"title":"","content":"Well, because i'm an twisted bastard i have no problem with other exalts trying to extract evocations from materials the character is neutral or disonant to - you just get 1 or 2 points of Limit, respectively, with each such use. And the limit points turn into extra motes - for evocation use only - if the character enters Limit Break (or whatever equivalent state fits). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:34:58-07:00","id":1318337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318263#post1318263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maximum Number of Evocations per Dot Rating? Where would I find that information? I Must have completely missed this...</div> </div> </div> </div>its in Arms, where they discuss how to build Artifacts, <br /> <br /> 3 dots is 10<br /> <br /> 4 dots is 15<br /> <br /> 5 dots is unlimited<br /> <br /> and N/A is also unlimited.<br /> <br /> Though do note this is only for individual evocation trees. Like you know how Artifacts can develop different Evocations depending on the wielder yeah? Those don't count towards the limit, its only the limit for the sole user. Also from what I remember reading from arms, very rarely was the list of Evocations hit the limit. So that gives you some breathing room","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T18:10:23-07:00","id":1318357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318326#post1318326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, because i'm an twisted bastard i have no problem with other exalts trying to extract evocations from materials the character is neutral or disonant to - you just get 1 or 2 points of Limit, respectively, with each such use. And the limit points turn into extra motes - for evocation use only - if the character enters Limit Break (or whatever equivalent state fits). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can learn Evocations from any artifact even if you're neutral or dissonant to them, they just aren't as strong as if you're Resonant. Are you adding an additional restriction to it or is this in the context of using Resonant level evocations when you would be Dissonant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T20:00:01-07:00","id":1318378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318357#post1318357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can learn Evocations from any artifact even if you're neutral or dissonant to them, they just aren't as strong as if you're Resonant. Are you adding an additional restriction to it or is this in the context of using Resonant level evocations when you would be Dissonant?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Using resonant-evocations when you would neutral or dissonant. The idea is not to restrict, but opening up tainted/dangerous options, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T03:01:15-07:00","id":1318632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318120#post1318120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solution: &amp;quot;Uh, guys, this is totally not Gnomon, this is its Blue Jade brother Chronos. Totally guys. Swear on me mum. Has all of Gnomon's Evocations and pretty much works the same way though.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I really don't &quot;get&quot; Resonance.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm this Moonsliver Reaver Daiklave is weak for my Dragon-Blooded. I'm going to homebrew the exact same Evocations onto a Black Jade Goremaul so I can get the Resonance bonuses.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T03:26:52-07:00","id":1318636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318167#post1318167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My house rule for Resonance is that you can be Resonant to any artifact that contains a magical material you are Resonant to.<br /> <br /> For instance, a weapon that is a Moonsilver and Jade Daiklave is resonant to Solars, Lunars, and Dragonblooded, plus any Exigent who is Resonant to Moonsilver or Jade.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To some extent, this is already true; there's a Moonsilver-and-Blue Jade umbrella which is resonant for both Lunars and Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> I think, for PCs, if say they're a Lunar who starts with a jade weapon they got from defeating the Dragonblood who killed their family, then I think it's easiest to say it happens to be a Jade-and-Moonsilver one which is Resonant for both DBs and Lunars.<br /> <br /> Other than Baaldam's limit idea for using forbidden materials, I think this is the best balanced; I do think Dissonance and Resonance are important thematically and in terms of making sure that, unlike DnD, you're not carting around 10 artefacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T03:38:33-07:00","id":1318640,"title":"","content":"I must say, and I don't mean to be agressive by asking that, but what's really the point with Resonance/Dissonance ? I don't find it very interesting after thinking about it but I never had the opportunity to really explore it, so what was the purpose of inventing those rules ? I don't get what they add to the dramas and flow of stories, and they just seem like mechanical arbitrary limitations who don't really favor good RP. Did I miss something, was there a developper that gave good insight on this sub-system ? Because I think I plan to straigth ignore them for most of my non Solar games","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T04:37:13-07:00","id":1318648,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Resonance and Dissonance</b><br /> <br /> If I had to venture a guess, I image the rules serve a niche protection and to give some meaning to the choice of magical materials. Limits and having to work around them foster creativity.<br /> I know, it feels counter intuitive. After all, most players hate to hear the words &quot;No&quot; about anything. But I think picking up a Artifact you are materially dissonant with can be a good role playing experience. Every artifact is unique, and is &quot;alive&quot; in a certain sense, and a given artifact can overrule material resonance if it fits the story. The Lunar that has to convince an Anathema Slaying Jade Daiklaive to accept it seems like it would be more interesting than simply adding another +3 Greatsword to the golfbag.<br /> <br /> Not to throw shade at bags of +3 Greatswords, but I think the devs wanted to do something a little different with magical items Exalted.<br /> <br /> The other option would have been unique material based bonuses, which could still be used as an alternative, but I think I would prefer it less. My tastes appreciate having to work towards goals and around obstacles, so I don't mind occasionally having one of my outrageous powers be slightly less-outrageous in a few circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-15-2019, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T05:26:45-07:00","id":1318655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318640#post1318640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, and I don't mean to be agressive by asking that, but what's really the point with Resonance/Dissonance ? I don't find it very interesting after thinking about it but I never had the opportunity to really explore it, so what was the purpose of inventing those rules ? I don't get what they add to the dramas and flow of stories, and they just seem like mechanical arbitrary limitations who don't really favor good RP. Did I miss something, was there a developper that gave good insight on this sub-system ? Because I think I plan to straigth ignore them for most of my non Solar games</div> </div> </div> </div>Various reasons.<br /> For Solars, obviously they decided &quot;yeah, just use whatever.&quot; (Which is a big change from 2nd ed, where Solars were weaker with non-orichalcum weapons). Not a big fan of that myself, but others like it.<br /> <br /> For Dragonblood, there's a genre thing. They are supposed to be using Jade weapons, not just any old material. Natural, earth-born magic is their wheelhouse, not the dark arts of necromancy, or the glow of the sun, or the mutability of the wyld.<br /> There's also power-theme. What I mean is, DB power is rather elemental. That's good, but it's also a weakness; they're not good at dealing with ghosts or spirits (they are, after all, the <i>Terrestrial</i> exalted, ie the earth-bound ones). Like sorcery, artefacts let them go out-of-theme, which makes them more powerful.<br /> Thus, artefacts that do similar things to stuff they can already do (instill emotion, walk on water, shoot fire, resist lightning, etc) are more powerful for them, but artefacts that let them do a bunch of new stuff (have a flying weapon that fights by itself, get fat bonuses on sorcery, eat ghosts for necro-power, etc) are weaker.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, there's something similar as for Dragonblood. Lunars, for example, are not good at manipulating elements, that's a weakness of theirs (sure, you can turn into a massive octopus, but you can't drown a ship in a whirlpool with some magic gestures, you have to fight the ship yourself). So for example, they are worse with a crossbow that makes whirlpools than a DB would be.<br /> But there's a couple of other things too.<br /> First, Jade is way more common than Moonsilver, and so you'd get Lunars outfitted mostly with Jade, which would detract from their aesthetic; they're supposed to be animalesque and silver, not outfitted in blue armour+weapons and shooting lightning.<br /> Secondly, when a Lunar group fights a Dragonblood Wyld Hunt, the ST doesn't really have to worry about giving the Dragonblood a bunch of artefacts.<br /> For example, one of my Lunar group has a moonsilver bow, and another has a moonsilver great axe. The bow less-so, but the great axe is a very important and thematic part of Olaf Keelbreaker's character; the haft is forged from his own walrus-fang that was knocked out by the Dragonblood who razed his village and left him for dead.<br /> Now, they're currently fighting their very first fight against a couple of Dragonblood who have no artefacts. But later, they'll fight DBs who do.<br /> What I don't want is for the PCs to kill five Dragonblood and just pick up five artefacts that, yeah, are mechanically beneficial, but ruin their aesthetic*. I definitely don't want Olaf Keelbreaker to find a weapon that's mechanically better to his tusk-axe, because I don't want him to have to choose between his backstory and some mechanical bonuses.<br /> <br /> *I don't want them to look like high-level MMO characters with completely mismatched item sets.<br /> <br /> But, while I can imagine that a couple of them may want to pick up free artefacts (after all, if you've got no evocations it makes no difference anyway), I'm not worried that they're going to swap their moonsilver items for jade, because jade is not mechanically better.<br /> And with the obviousness of artefacts, the attunement costs, and finally lack of resonance as the cherry on top, I think they're not going to cover themselves in jade, even if they do loot 10 artefacts. I suspect that maybe one of them will pick up a jade weapon and armour, and the rest will just sell the stuff, gift it, or bury it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The same things apply to Abyssals and Sidereals. Can you imagine an Abyssal covered in bling-gold light-shooting armor and weapons? Seems a bit silly. I mean, the current system means that you can... it's just not as good as using Soulsteel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T09:57:16-07:00","id":1318701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318636#post1318636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To some extent, this is already true; there's a Moonsilver-and-Blue Jade umbrella which is resonant for both Lunars and Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> I think, for PCs, if say they're a Lunar who starts with a jade weapon they got from defeating the Dragonblood who killed their family, then I think it's easiest to say it happens to be a Jade-and-Moonsilver one which is Resonant for both DBs and Lunars.<br /> <br /> Other than Baaldam's limit idea for using forbidden materials, I think this is the best balanced; I do think Dissonance and Resonance are important thematically and in terms of making sure that, unlike DnD, you're not carting around 10 artefacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But I was using the rule before that Umbrella and I expand it to every artifact of multiple origins instead of specifically the Umbrella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T10:41:11-07:00","id":1318709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318632#post1318632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I really don't &quot;get&quot; Resonance.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmm this Moonsliver Reaver Daiklave is weak for my Dragon-Blooded. I'm going to homebrew the exact same Evocations onto a Black Jade Goremaul so I can get the Resonance bonuses.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some Artifacts lend themselves better to this kind of translation than others. Gnomon is VERY difficult to translate to other materials, though you could make a case for Moonsilver or Orichalcum, but the Hawk Star's Jess could be translated to Blue Jade. In the end I assume it's there to make going outside of your splat's themes a less potent possibility than throwing yourself fully behind them, but going outside them gets you more varied powers you wouldn't otherwise have. That said, we have too little non-Orichalcum Artifacts to go around with non-Solars, so for now I'd be fine with just translating them to other materials to gain Resonance and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T10:55:30-07:00","id":1318711,"title":"","content":"I think there's over 20 Jade artefacts, and about 20 moonsilver artefacts. That seems like plenty.<br /> <br /> Starmetal and soulsteel are very restricted though. But if you're playing a Sidereal or Abyssal, I think you've got bigger mechanical hurdles to deal with than lack of Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T11:04:18-07:00","id":1318714,"title":"","content":"If there's anything that's missing to me it's armor. Especially Jade armor, which we only have 2 examples of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T11:22:05-07:00","id":1318717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318711#post1318711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's over 20 Jade artefacts, and about 20 moonsilver artefacts. That seems like plenty.<br /> <br /> Starmetal and soulsteel are very restricted though. But if you're playing a Sidereal or Abyssal, I think you've got bigger mechanical hurdles to deal with than lack of Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Jade Artifacts in the DB book are not exactly great in their majority, and having to rule out the whole Heirloom thing to allow Outcastes or Lookshians or w/e those Artifacts is a bit messy, let alone the whole &quot;Evocations are 12 XP&quot; deal that makes Dissonant or Neutral Artifacts even less desirable. Moonsilver ones are great mostly, with some exceptions, so Lunars have more freedom when it comes to picking those. Siddies and Abyssals don't have that many mechanical hurdles that I know of, if anything they're doing pretty great; both get Celestial Sorcery, one gets Void Necromancy, both have dope Artifacts ready for them in Arms, both get Mastery and access to SMA and one of them has SMA Mastery-like benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T12:37:22-07:00","id":1318727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318717#post1318717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siddies and Abyssals don't have that many mechanical hurdles that I know of, if anything they're doing pretty great; both get Celestial Sorcery, one gets Void Necromancy, both have dope Artifacts ready for them in Arms, both get Mastery and access to SMA and one of them has SMA Mastery-like benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they don't have books, that seems kind of an issue.<br /> <br /> But if you're happy with them, great. Sounds like you're happy with Lunars too.<br /> <br /> For DBs, Heirloom is a bonus for Dynasts, it's not a penalty for Outcastes. You buy the first charm, like you would for most Artefacts.<br /> (And... maybe you can claim your Outcaste is descended from a certain dynasty on their great-grandma's side)<br /> <br /> But I will agree with you that the artefacts in WFHW aren't that exciting. I mean, I guess that's subjective, but I didn't find them very exciting for the most part. Some I kind of liked. But the ones in Arms and Lunars were better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-15-2019, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T13:15:59-07:00","id":1318730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318709#post1318709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Some Artifacts lend themselves better to this kind of translation than others. Gnomon is VERY difficult to translate to other materials, though you could make a case for Moonsilver or Orichalcum</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Not-Gnomon was forged by the architect of the Usurpation to represent the covenant between the Sidreals as the agents of heaven and the Terrestrials who would inherit Creation.<br /> <br /> It is said that a borough of the purest green jade, harvested from the Elemental Pole of Wood was grafted onto one of the sacred Peach Trees of Immortality in the Heavenly City. The tree was faithfully watered with Perfected Water for seven nights until viens of blue and black jade appeared in the borough. The limb was then ritually burned with the Flames of Kesiah and quenched in powdered earth from mount Meru until veins of white and red jade appeared. When this artifical limb finally bore fruit, it was severed from the tree by Chejop Kejak. Such was the Sidreal's understanding of endings, that fate itself failed to realise the borough was no longer part of the tree.<br /> <br /> The blue jade in this wrackstaff allows it's wielder to anticipate the intent of its wielders opponents, the red jade speeds the wielder's movements, the black jade eases the flow of martial arts and turns the tide of time itself whilst the white jade grants the perfect calm and clarity needed to seemingly immobilise the world around its wielder.<br /> <br /> But it is the living Essence of Green Jade that grants Not-Gnomen its greatest power -- the ability to grow Peaches of Immortality.<br /> <br /> Not-Gnomen is seeped in Heavenly Essence, and carries with it the enduring stamp of Chejop Kejak's Celestial Essence. Any Sidereal Exalted or god who works for the Bureau of Destiny believes the staff\u2019s wielder is a legitimate agent of Heaven. This is equivalent to a Minor Tie of trust.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-15-2019, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T13:26:09-07:00","id":1318733,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with most of that explanation except the &quot;tides of time&quot;. Time-control just isn't a jade thing, even if you metaphorically describe it as water-like.<br /> <br /> Certainly growing a magic peach of life seems fine for green jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T13:57:14-07:00","id":1318740,"title":"","content":"I have been musing around an idea of a green jade staff that does give a sort of immortality and a longer life. Specifically the jade staff of the Dragon-Blooded in Dreams of the First Age who lived for over thousands of years from sheer enlightenment. That is see as a pretty dope legend to turn into an Artifact","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T08:57:35-07:00","id":1318870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318727#post1318727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they don't have books, that seems kind of an issue.<br /> <br /> But if you're happy with them, great. Sounds like you're happy with Lunars too.<br /> <br /> For DBs, Heirloom is a bonus for Dynasts, it's not a penalty for Outcastes. You buy the first charm, like you would for most Artefacts.<br /> (And... maybe you can claim your Outcaste is descended from a certain dynasty on their great-grandma's side)<br /> <br /> But I will agree with you that the artefacts in WFHW aren't that exciting. I mean, I guess that's subjective, but I didn't find them very exciting for the most part. Some I kind of liked. But the ones in Arms and Lunars were better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am definitely happy with Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:06:43-07:00","id":1318884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318740#post1318740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been musing around an idea of a green jade staff that does give a sort of immortality and a longer life. Specifically the jade staff of the Dragon-Blooded in Dreams of the First Age who lived for over thousands of years from sheer enlightenment. That is see as a pretty dope legend to turn into an Artifact</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, but sounds like more of a simple benefit that would go better with a hearthstone perhaps - in fact 1e had one that would fit, the Gem of Immortality, if memory tricks me not.<br /> As an artifact, what kind of evocations' tree could spring from that as a starting point, or lead into that as its pinnacle effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T10:14:23-07:00","id":1318887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318884#post1318884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting, but sounds like more of a simple benefit that would go better with a hearthstone perhaps - in fact 1e had one that would fit, the Gem of Immortality, if memory tricks me not.<br /> As an artifact, what kind of evocations' tree could spring from that as a starting point, or lead into that as its pinnacle effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have the effect as the capstone, with the other evocations building up to it. As for the other Evocations, I have some ideas. Mainly on those of self reflection and enlightenment. Building off from some concepts in Integrity and Survival","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T23:11:12-07:00","id":1319008,"title":"","content":"If a player in your gaming group really wants a resonant effect - or wants to buy off a dissonant effect - we usually do it as a repurchase, or a new Evocation that enhances the existing one. So far, it is a solution everyone is happy with, but in our group we also tend to value style over substance for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T05:26:53-07:00","id":1319439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1319008#post1319008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a player in your gaming group really wants a resonant effect - or wants to buy off a dissonant effect - we usually do it as a repurchase or a new Evocation that enhances the existing one. So far, it is a solution everyone is happy with, but in our group, we also tend to value style over substance for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is really worth to purchase a whole evocation just to get rid of dissonance ou getting resonance? I mean, resonance is usually good, but rarely that good. Perhaps if those evocations did something more than just upping the resonance, but then we go to the custom evocation land again. For more mechanically-minded players, this would seem to be just the same as not allowing the option in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T07:15:10-07:00","id":1319454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1318120#post1318120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solution: &quot;Uh, guys, this is totally not Gnomon, this is its Blue Jade brother Chronos. Totally guys. Swear on me mum. Has all of Gnomon's Evocations and pretty much works the same way though.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or learn Wood-aspected Evocations for Gnomon that grow some other kind of fruit. One that won't be as powerful, but one that can be grown far more often.<br /> <br /> Can you survive one whole year between each Celestial Peach? Surviving a whole year would be easier with <i>twelve </i>Marvelous Peaches that heal injuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T07:40:06-07:00","id":1319458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1318100-houserules-for-artifacts-and-resonance?p=1319439#post1319439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But is really worth to purchase a whole evocation just to get rid of dissonance ou getting resonance? I mean, resonance is usually good, but rarely that good. Perhaps if those evocations did something more than just upping the resonance, but then we go to the custom evocation land again. For more mechanically-minded players, this would seem to be just the same as not allowing the option in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It would not always be worth it. In the example I am thinking about the player with a Dragon-Blooded character owns Heartsbalm and wanted the resonant effect for Heart-Forged Aegis, extending the duration from one turn to one scene, which he had no hesitation with paying for a new Evocation to gain.<br /> <br /> Some resonant effects I myself consider so minor I would never expend an Evocation slot to achieve it (the above example I would be OK with, though), but if the players are happy with it, who am I to say no.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}